Date: Wed, 28 Oct 1998 08:46:08 -0500
From: Aaron Bauch <aaron.bauch@digital.com>
Subject: 66MHz DIMM support on RX? (was :Re:Here what I figured!)
To: "'AlphaNT Mail List'" <AlphaNT@alphant.com>
Reply-To: AlphaNT Mail List <AlphaNT@AlphaNT.com>

The RX, like the SX uses standard 168 Pin DIMMs.  The SX memory bus runs at
66MHz so it generally uses slower DIMMs while the RX runs its memory bus at
75 or 83MHz.  To do this it typically uses industry standard PC100 DIMMs.
If you want to use use the old DIMMs the bus would need to run no faster
than 66MHz, giving up about half of the benefit of the faster memory bus
support on the RX (there are other factors that improve the bandwidth as
well, even at the same frequency).  I don't believe that this is currently
planned as a supported feature but if there is sufficient demand it is
technically feasible.  I would be interested in feedback from anyone on the
list with an opinion one way or the other on this.

Aaron

