After reading all the press releases, position statements, and others' opinions, I see no need to change the name AlphaNT to anything else at this time or anytime in the foreseeable future.

Changing the name to Alpha2000 would be temporary, needing a change again in 2001 or 2002 or...

NT stands for New Technology, which is what we're promoting.

Even Microsoft is keeping NT in it's tagline.

I can't think of anything that describes what we are trying to promote better than those 7 letters.  It's concise and clear in its implications.  Anything else would be Microsoft sponsored confusion.

As computer professionals, I think we'll all know what we mean by "NT" in the year 2003.  While I'm interested in reaching beyond this audience, I'm also interested in the "brand equity" and letting newcomers know that we've had a competitive advantage since 1993.

If anyone has suggestions for a new name that can carry us beyond 2000, I'll be taking them for the next couple of years.  Feel free to send me email with your new name suggestions.

Regards,
Aaron
