>Just a quick note to clear up some of the confusion; on  an EB164 (Alpha
>machine) it is not possible to have ISA and PCI IRQ conflicts.  These IRQs
>are routed differently. PCI interrupts directly to the CPU whereas ISA
>interrupts via the PIC (Priority Interrupt Controller). Therefore, ISA and
>PCI IRQ conflicts are impossible and this is not causing your problem.
>Something else is going on.  Either the network card is bad or something is
>amiss with the network configuration.  I would check the network card in
>another system to verify that it works properly.  If so, then I would
>uninstall the network on the EB164 and then re-install the network.  Also,
I
>believe  the DE500-BA had problems with autonegotiating between 10 and 100
>mb/s.  If your current network connection is set to Autosense; manually
>change the setting in the Network/Adapter/ Properties to the type of
network
>connection and speed  that your network is capable of.
>

