Thanks Peter for the kind words about UltraBac -- always appreciated.

The original poster was inquiring about which backup software had the
largest market share, as if this would be an indicator to the quality of
the software.  I don't think that UltraBac will ever have the largest
market share in the backup market -- BEI as a company do not have that
hunger for world dominance, and stomach for double-dealing,
back-stabbing that seems to be a pre-requisite these days to be a
billion dollar corporation.  However, we remain focused on creating very
reliable high-quality backup software for WindowsNT on all platforms --
that is all we do.  All of our energies are focused on developing,
maintaining, and most importantly supporting, UltraBac.   The press have
not completely ignored us (we have won "Editor's Choice" awards and
there are links to some nice reviews of the products on our website) --
but being a small company, not every magazine are aware of our existance
when they decide to review NT backup software, and hence, we are often
left out of the evaluation.  We tend to accumulate very loyal happy
customers for those people who are able to see past what is a very
simple interface to a flexible product.

General Motors, Microsoft, K-Mart all enjoy significant market share in
their respective industries, however, I'm sure that everyone would agree
that there is room for other competitors who offer different ordering of
priorites.  When making a decision on any product it comes down to:
price, performance, reliability, brand name reputation, features,
ease-of-use -- you simply pick the vendor that closely matches your own
set of priorities.

Dave, the Legato solution that you are running is good software.  It
tends to be rather expensive, but is one of the few remaining
applications that can handle the diverse range of platforms that you are
running.  My personal preference would be to let Unix backup Unix and NT
backup NT, and in this environment you could possibly let Legato backup
your Unix boxes, and either UltraBac or BackupExec backup your NT
systems.

Regards,

Paul Bunn, BEI, 425-644-6000
Microsoft MVP - WindowsNT
