From Paul@ULTRABAC.com Thu, 29 Oct 1998 16:43:16 -0800
Message-ID: <911379A952ACD0119A4D006097A0EDCF4E1980@INQUISITOR>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 1998 16:43:16 -0800
From: Paul Bunn <Paul@ULTRABAC.com>
Subject: RE: Application Log
To: 'AlphaNT Mail List' <AlphaNT@AlphaNT.com>
Reply-To: AlphaNT Mail List <AlphaNT@AlphaNT.com>

Applications can write information/warning/error messages to the
Application/Security/System event logs at will.  Run Event Viewer
(eventvwr.exe) to view the logs, and change the settings.  The easiest
method is to allow the overwriting of events as necessary to eliminate
this message-box that you are seeing, but this is dangerous as if an
application is in mortal peril, it's cries in the event log will
probably go unnoticed.  I'd probably advise increasing the logs' sizes
so that enough history is maintained to allow reasonble diagnosing of
problems.

Regards,

Paul Bunn, BEI, 425-644-6000
Microsoft MVP - WindowsNT
http://www.ultrabac.com

